  "body": "**Blocked by:** #99\n\n## Context\n\nThe ten system databases do not include the three databases required by Inbox processing.\n\n## Task\n\nSeed database keys `inbox`, `inboxItemTypes`, and `processingProposals` with localized display metadata. Inbox has mandatory user-owned `date` and `time`, user-owned `text`, nullable user-owned relation `type`, and system-owned relation `journalDay`. The client must supply date and time; the server must never replace them with its current date. Resolve `journalDay` at write time through the existing lazy Journal-day mechanism. Seed proposal properties exactly: `kind` (`inbox|transcript`), nullable `sourceInbox`/`sourceTranscript`, `fingerprint`, `proposal`, `history`, `status`, nullable `resultItemId`, and nullable `resultLabel`. Add `GET /api/inbox-types`, returning active types as `{ id, emoji, label }`; relations store the id, never emoji.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Baseline schemas, ownership, canonical keys, Journal relation, and type listing.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Processing behavior, type lifecycle, proposal endpoints, and Shortcuts UI.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Repeated seed is idempotent and validates the exact schema.\n- Missing date or time is rejected; delayed capture preserves supplied values.\n- Journal day is lazily resolved once and relation integrity is enforced.\n- An Inbox item without `type` can be created and later enters `needsClarification`; renaming a type's emoji does not break Inbox relations.\n",
